st surveys suggest.", "watch": "Whether Andrews' fundraising advantage converts into sustained polling leads or outside spending shifts the race in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Darline Graham (R) is running."]}, "overview": "South Carolina's special Senate race pits appointed incumbent Darline Graham, who won the GOP runoff to replace her brother Lindsey Graham, against Democrat Annie Andrews. The state leans Republican by about eight points, and most expert ratings land at Likely or Lean R, though a few call it Safe R.\n\nThe polling picture is unusually close for South Carolina: late-September surveys from InsiderAdvantage and Trafalgar show Graham ahead by only one point, and averages put the race at roughly a one-to-two point Graham edge. Andrews has raised over $10 million to Graham's under $400 thousand, though outside groups have spent heavily for the incumbent. Prediction markets still give Andrews only about a 12-17% chance, suggesting skepticism that the polling tightness holds. The forecast expects Graham to win by around four points with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1565, "margin": -5.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2122, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2115, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2143, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1474, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2135, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2708, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2623, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2878, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2627, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}]}